From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:53:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: set default ASan options

tapdisk is spawned by tap-ctl, from SM, so ASAN_OPTIONS can't easily
be set in its environment, and libasan reads it before main(). In an
ASan build, provide the defaults with __asan_default_options():

- handle_abort, to get the stack of an abort() such as a failed ASSERT,
  whose message is otherwise lost with the buffered syslog;
- symbolize=0, since symbolizing in the crashing process can crash
  again and hide the report;
- log_path, to keep the report whatever stderr is redirected to.

ASAN_OPTIONS still overrides these defaults.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/tapdisk2.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk2.c b/drivers/tapdisk2.c
index c0f9d013..3a5087fd 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk2.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk2.c
@@ -48,6 +48,22 @@
 void tdnbd_fdreceiver_start();
 void tdnbd_fdreceiver_stop();
 
+#ifdef __SANITIZE_ADDRESS__
+/*
+ * Default ASan options, read by libasan before main(): tapdisk is spawned
+ * by tap-ctl, whose environment we don't control. ASAN_OPTIONS still
+ * overrides them.
+ * - handle_abort: report the stack of an abort(), e.g. a failed ASSERT
+ * - symbolize=0: don't symbolize in the crashing process, which can crash
+ *   again; symbolize offline with addr2line
+ * - log_path: write the report to <log_path>.<pid>, whatever stderr is
+ */
+const char *__asan_default_options(void)
+{
+	return "handle_abort=1:symbolize=0:log_path=/var/log/blktap/asan";
+}
+#endif
+
 static void
 usage(const char *app, int err)
 {
